    "scenario": "You are asked to evaluate a 1 y.o. previously healthy child who underwent repair of cleft palate and who is still on positive pressure ventilation (PPV) in the post- anesthesia care unit (PACU). The end tidal CO2 is 32 mmHg, while the arterial CO2 is 42 mmHg. Which of the following most closely represents the physiological dead space?",
