    "scenario": "A 1-year-old boy is admitted to the PICU from the emergency department (ED) for extreme pallor, tachypnea and tachycardia. The family arrived from overseas two weeks ago and the father states that the patient may have “a blood disease.” He appears “fussy” with P 141, respiratory rate (RR) 34, BP 108/65, T 37, pulse oximetry 100% in RA. His initial hemoglobin is 2.9 g %. What should be your initial step in the management of this patient?",
