    "scenario": "A 4-week-old neonate with acute respiratory failure on mechanical ventilation with FiO2 of 0.80 is being transported from Chile where the barometric pressure is 500 mmHg to Boston where the barometric pressure is 747 mmHg. The PaO2 on the blood gas and the SpO2 have been reported to be satisfactory. What would be the appropriate FiO2 in order to maintain the same PaO2 and SpO2 after the baby arrives at the new location if the PaCO2 is 40?",
