    "scenario": "A 15 y.o. with moderate persistent asthma is seen in the ED for URTI symptoms for 2 days, which progressed to cough, wheezing and respiratory distress last night. Despite therapy with continuous albuterol nebulization, systemic steroids, IV mg sulfate he continued to deteriorate. 4 hours after admission to the PICU he was noted to have depressed mental status; ABGs: pH 7.01, PaCO2 85 mmHg, PaO2 98 (while on continuous albuterol nebulization) and bicarbonate of 17 mEq/L. Which of the following is true?",
