    "scenario": "An 8 y.o. (28 kg) with respiratory failure due to ARDS following motor vehicle collision is on conventional mechanical ventilation (CMV) with a tidal volume (TV) of 200 mL, synchronized intermittent mandatory ventilation (SIMV) rate of 18, PEEP of 12 and FiO2 of 0.80 with SpO2 of 87%. A pulmonary artery catheter is in place and his most recent cardiac index is 2.5 L/min/m2. DO2 will be increased most by:",
