    "id": 5146,
    "title": "American Physician Institute Q129",
    "scenario": "A 10-year-old is admitted for generalized tonic-clonic seizures treated successfully by Emergency Medical Services with IV lorazepam. Initial Cerebrospinal Fluid (CSF) analysis reveals 3 white blood cells and normal protein and glucose. Viral and bacterial PCR are negative. He continues to be unresponsive with periods of sinus tachycardia (124 beats/min), but does not have focal neurological signs. Of the following, the most appropriate next step in the management of this patient is:",
