    "correctAnswer": "C",
    "correctAnswerText": "Hypertonic saline",
    "explanation": "Diluted formula causes water intoxication and hyponatremia. Seizures are typical below 115 mEq/L, and the threshold is lowered below 125. Symptomatic hyponatremia is an emergency best treated with hypertonic (3%) saline, and benzodiazepines often fail until sodium is corrected.",
