    "id": 5154,
    "title": "American Physician Institute Q134",
    "scenario": "You are evaluating a 16-year-old who is admitted with vertigo, dysphagia and vomiting. Physical examination shows deviation of the uvula to the right side and dysmetria. Of the following, the most likely involved blood vessel is:",
