    "correctAnswer": "E",
    "correctAnswerText": "Pralidoxime reverses muscarinic effects more effectively than nicotinic effects",
    "explanation": "Pralidoxime reactivates acetylcholinesterase mainly at nicotinic sites (it reverses muscle weakness). Atropine treats the muscarinic (DUMBBELS) effects. The statement that pralidoxime reverses muscarinic effects better is therefore incorrect. Sarin 'ages' and binds irreversibly, so oximes must be given early.",
