    "scenario": "An 8 y.o. boy (BSA 0.9 m2) has sepsis with MODS and is on mechanical ventilation via a cuffed ETT and is being sedated and paralyzed with FiO2 0.6, TV 220, SIMV 25, PEEP 6 with a flow rate of 30 L/min. The PIP is 36. One second following airway occlusion the pressure measured is 28 cm H2O. Vital signs include: P 121 bpm, BP 115/56, temperature 39.6 oC. ABGs: pH 7.29, PO2 105, PaCO2 34 and sat 99%. Mixed venous blood gas: pH 7.21, PO2 43, PaCO2 37 and sat 74%. CBC shows a hemoglobin of 7.6 g/dL, WBC 4 with 35% bands and a platelet count of 73,000/mm3. Cardiac output measured by thermodilution technique is 3.5 L/min, CVP is 8, PAP 36/20 (25), PAOP is 5. What is the static lung-chest wall compliance in this child?",
