    "correctAnswer": "E",
    "correctAnswerText": "Lung compliance is 16 mL/cm H2O",
    "explanation": "Driving pressure = 38 − 15 = 23 cm H₂O. Compliance ≈ 380/23 ≈ 16 mL/cm H₂O, which is the key's answer. The circuit compresses only 2 × 23 ≈ 46 mL, so most of the tidal volume reaches the patient. Correcting for this gives about 14.5 mL/cm H₂O.",
